      "notes": "All claims are well-supported by their quoted evidence. Tier assignments are appropriate: stated claims draw from policy text, measurable claims from parliamentary/government sources, projected claims clearly flagged. The E11 claim that the 2016 Bill 'did not succeed' slightly overstates the quote ('did not detail its progress or outcome'), but the rationale is careful to say it 'stalled' rather than asserting failure as fact, and the verdict's biggest_unknown acknowledges this \u2014 borderline but not blocking. The E16 RCN figure is cited from a secondary aggregator (vertexaisearch), which is a minor sourcing weakness but not blocking given corroboration from other sources. Direction 'improves' is justified by two distinct documented equality gaps. Magnitude 'moderate' is reasonable given one proven delivery model (Scotland) and one legally untested element. No lever leakage, party-blind throughout, no false balance issues."
